# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# The golden fixtures are compared byte-for-byte (v4 spec §14.3), so Git must not translate
# their line endings in either direction — some baselines are legitimately stored with CRLF.
# That rule now lives in the fixtures repo's own .gitattributes, because the fixtures are a
# separate private repo cloned into the gitignored goldenFixtures/. Nothing here governs
# them; if a fresh fixtures clone ever comes up with every baseline differing, that file is
# what to check.

# The committed fixtures are measured, not just parsed. The pathological project's diagnostic
# snapshot records opening lengths in characters, and CL0710/CL0711 compare those lengths
# against the platform's 4,000-character cap — so a checkout that turns LF into CRLF adds one
# byte per line and moves numbers that the snapshot has pinned. Under `text=auto` alone that
# is exactly what happens on any machine with core.autocrlf=true, which is the Git for Windows
# default: the fixture is committed LF, checked out CRLF, and the suite fails on a fresh clone
# for a reason that has nothing to do with the compiler.
#
# `eol=lf` keeps normalizing to LF on commit and additionally forces LF on checkout, so the
# working file matches the blob the snapshot was generated from on every platform.
/__tests__/fixtures/** text eol=lf
/test/** text eol=lf
